Source: patchman-client
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Marcus Furlong <furlongm@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), golang-go (>= 1.21), dh-golang, dh-python, python3
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/furlongm/patchman-client
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/furlongm/patchman-client.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/furlongm/patchman-client

Package: patchman-client
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, patchman-client-bash | patchman-client-python | patchman-client-go
Description: Patchman client - meta-package with hooks
 Patchman client sends system package information to a patchman server.
 .
 This meta-package installs package manager hooks and depends on one of the
 client implementations (bash, python, or go).
 .
 The default implementation is bash (most tested). Use update-alternatives
 to switch between implementations:
   update-alternatives --config patchman-client

Package: patchman-client-bash
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, bash, curl, coreutils, gawk, grep, sed
Recommends: jq
Provides: patchman-client-impl
Description: Patchman client - bash implementation
 Patchman client sends system package information to a patchman server.
 .
 This package provides the bash implementation of the patchman client.
 It is the most tested and recommended implementation.
 .
 jq is recommended for protocol 2 (REST/JSON) support.

Package: patchman-client-python
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3-requests
Provides: patchman-client-impl
Description: Patchman client - Python implementation
 Patchman client sends system package information to a patchman server.
 .
 This package provides the Python implementation of the patchman client.
 It uses the REST API (protocol 2) only.

Package: patchman-client-go
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Provides: patchman-client-impl
Description: Patchman client - Go implementation
 Patchman client sends system package information to a patchman server.
 .
 This package provides the Go implementation of the patchman client.
 It is a compiled binary with no runtime dependencies.
 It uses the REST API (protocol 2) only.

Package: patchman-openscap
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, openscap-scanner, ssg-debian | ssg-debderived
Description: Patchman OpenSCAP compliance scanner
 Runs OpenSCAP CIS benchmark scans and writes structured JSON results
 to disk for inclusion in patchman client reports.
 .
 Auto-detects the OS and selects the appropriate SCAP datastream.
 Results are picked up by patchman-client on the next report submission.
 .
 Requires scap-security-guide content (ssg-debian, ssg-debderived,
 or scap-security-guide) for the target OS.
